@page
@model InfiniteAfternoon.Pages.IndexModel

<div id="titlecontainer" aria-hidden="true">
    <h1>Infinite <br /> Afternoon</h1>
</div>

<div class="dropscanvas" aria-hidden="true">

</div>

<div class="themiddle second" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div class="themiddle third" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<button type="button" class="uitoggle" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Hide the controls">hide</button>

<p class="invitation">Ambient music that never repeats itself.</p>

<div class="themiddle">
    <button id="start" type="button" aria-label="Play"></button>

    <div class="volume">
        <input id="volumecontrol" type="range" min="0" max="110" step="1" value="100" aria-label="Volume" />
        <span class="vollabel" aria-hidden="true">vol</span>
    </div>

    <div class="controls">
        <button type="button" class="openinfo" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="about">about</button>
        <button type="button" class="sleeptimer" aria-label="Sleep timer off">timer</button>
        <button type="button" class="midilink" aria-label="Play along with a MIDI keyboard">midi</button>
    </div>

    <div class="infocontainer" hidden>
        <div class="info hidden" id="about">
            @* the panel covers the button that opened it, so it carries its own way out *@
            <button type="button" class="closeinfo" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>

            <p class="phonehint">When listening on a phone, please unmute your device.</p>

            <h2>infinite afternoon</h2>
            <h3>What is Infinite Afternoon?</h3>
            <p>Infinite Afternoon gives you always-changing ambient music, available on the web.</p>
            <p>All notes and effects are played at randomly selected intervals. Due to these intervals, every user will hear completely unique interplay between notes, no matter how many times you refresh or how long you leave it open. </p>
            <p>Infinite Afternoon is inspired by Brian Eno's piece 'Thursday Afternoon'. Eno's piece is ultimately limited in time due to the nature of music distribution, while Inifinite Afternoon could potentially go on forever.</p>

            <h3>What techniques are used to make Infinite Afternoon?</h3>
            <p>I have created the samples with Ableton Live.</p>
            <p>The page is created with HTML/CSS and JavaScript. In JavaScript I use the Web Audio API to play and manipulate the audio files.</p>
            <p>The 'drops' you see are aligned with the panning of the notes.</p>

            <h3>Is Infinite Afternoon using AI-generated music?</h3>
            <p>No. All sounds were created by me, and the timing is done based on rules. Claude did help with some of the programming.</p>

            <h3>Can I play along?</h3>
            <p>Yes! Click or tap anywhere to drop a note. On a keyboard, A&ndash;H play the high notes and Z&ndash;B the low piano notes. You can even plug in a MIDI keyboard and enable it with the 'midi' button &mdash; every key is pitched from the original samples.</p>

            <h3>Can I get in contact?</h3>
            <p>Email me at <a href="mailto:afternoon@erwinvk.nl">afternoon@erwinvk.nl</a> for anything! Maybe we can team up to make something great. Or maybe you have an idea, or something is not working correctly. Let me know!</p>

            <p>Also check out <a href="https://erwinvankester.nl">erwinvankester.nl</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="sky dusk" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div class="sky night" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div class="sky dawn" aria-hidden="true"></div>

@* the horizon is drawn from what you have actually heard — see site.js *@
<div class="wavescontainer" aria-hidden="true">
    <canvas class="waves"></canvas>
</div>

